	<script type="application/ld+json" class="yoast-schema-graph">{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#article","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/"},"author":{"name":"Laura Bashar","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#\/schema\/person\/5a3ebcca21aea0ad7f6b5def103acd37"},"headline":"Dutch Oven Chili with Cornbread","datePublished":"2009-08-03T20:37:00+00:00","dateModified":"2025-05-01T01:34:05+00:00","wordCount":2054,"commentCount":13,"publisher":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#organization"},"image":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#primaryimage"},"thumbnailUrl":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2009\/08\/campfire_chili_cornbread_1200-2.jpg","keywords":["black beans","chiles","jalapeno","tomatoes"],"articleSection":["beef","campfire cooking","dutch oven recipes","ground beef","Main Course","turkey"],"inLanguage":"en-US","potentialAction":[{"@type":"CommentAction","name":"Comment","target":["https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#respond"]}]},{"@type":["WebPage","FAQPage"],"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/","name":"Dutch Oven Chili with Cornbread - Family Spice","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#primaryimage"},"image":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#primaryimage"},"thumbnailUrl":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2009\/08\/campfire_chili_cornbread_1200-2.jpg","datePublished":"2009-08-03T20:37:00+00:00","dateModified":"2025-05-01T01:34:05+00:00","description":"Whether you are camping or at home, make this Dutch oven chili with cornbread (aka cowboy chili) where you bake them together in the same pot!","breadcrumb":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":[{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#faq-question-1657487514911"},{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#faq-question-1657487732053"}],"inLanguage":"en-US","potentialAction":[{"@type":"ReadAction","target":["https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/"]}]},{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#primaryimage","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2009\/08\/campfire_chili_cornbread_1200-2.jpg","contentUrl":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2009\/08\/campfire_chili_cornbread_1200-2.jpg","width":1200,"height":1800,"caption":"Top view of a cast iron dutch oven with chili and cornbread in it"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Courses","item":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/courses\/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Main Course","item":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/courses\/main-course-courses\/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"Dutch Oven Chili with Cornbread"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#website","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/","name":"Family Spice","description":"World Cuisine for the Whole Family","publisher":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#organization"},"potentialAction":[{"@type":"SearchAction","target":{"@type":"EntryPoint","urlTemplate":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/?s={search_term_string}"},"query-input":{"@type":"PropertyValueSpecification","valueRequired":true,"valueName":"search_term_string"}}],"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#organization","name":"Family Spice","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#\/schema\/logo\/image\/","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/new_FS_logo_2020_SQ.jpg","contentUrl":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/new_FS_logo_2020_SQ.jpg","width":257,"height":258,"caption":"Family Spice"},"image":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#\/schema\/logo\/image\/"},"sameAs":["https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/familyspice","https:\/\/x.com\/familyspice","https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/familyspice\/","http:\/\/pinterest.com\/familyspice","https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/channel\/UC3Pk0r7ITtSVlWEHk1lnHKQ"]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/#\/schema\/person\/5a3ebcca21aea0ad7f6b5def103acd37","name":"Laura Bashar","sameAs":["https:\/\/familyspice.com\/about-me\/","https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/familyspice\/","https:\/\/x.com\/familyspice"],"url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/author\/laura\/"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#faq-question-1657487514911","position":1,"url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#faq-question-1657487514911","name":"Can I make chili in my cast iron Dutch oven?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The cast iron Dutch oven is perfect for making chili. Always start with a well seasoned pot and you can cook most anything in your cast ironware. The walls of the Dutch oven retain heat beautifully giving you even heat for whatever you are cooking inside of it.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#faq-question-1657487732053","position":2,"url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#faq-question-1657487732053","name":"What do you cook in a cast iron Dutch oven?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can cook most anything in a cast iron Dutch oven, like stews to soups and chili. You can also bake bread, cakes, cobblers and cookies and in a Dutch oven too. Think of it as a small oven and you will see that you can make most anything in this versatile pot.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Recipe","name":"Dutch Oven Cornbread Chili","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Laura Bashar | Family Spice"},"description":"Whether you are camping or at home, make something special like this Dutch oven chili with cornbread where you bake the cornbread in the same pot as your chili! Also known as cowboy chili, you are sure to be a hit at the campground.","datePublished":"2009-08-03T13:37:00+00:00","image":["https:\/\/familyspice.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2009\/08\/campfire_chili_cornbread_1200-2.jpg"],"recipeYield":["8"],"prepTime":"PT15M","cookTime":"PT45M","totalTime":"PT60M","recipeIngredient":["1 tbsp extra virgin olive oil","1  onion (diced)","1  red bell pepper (seeded & diced)","1  anaheim chile (seeded & diced)","1  jalapeño pepper (seeded & diced)","1 1\/2 lb ground turkey","4  garlic cloves (minced)","2 tbsp chile powder","1 tsp cumin","1\/2 tsp salt","15 oz canned black beans (drained an rinsed)","15 oz canned tomato sauce","15 oz canned diced tomatoes","3 oz chipotle chile in adobo sauce","4 oz green chiles (canned, drained & diced)","1\/2 cup water (if needed)","1  box of cornbread mix"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"In a fire ring or other fire-safe container add 35 charcoal briquettes.","name":"In a fire ring or other fire-safe container add 35 charcoal briquettes.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Light the briquettes and allow to heat up for approximately 20-30 minutes.","name":"Light the briquettes and allow to heat up for approximately 20-30 minutes.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"When flames are down and coals are hot, place over the hot coals a 10-inch cast iron Dutch oven.","name":"When flames are down and coals are hot, place over the hot coals a 10-inch cast iron Dutch oven.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Add olive oil into Dutch oven.","name":"Add olive oil into Dutch oven.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Stir in diced onions, bell peppers, anaheim chile and jalapeño pepper.","name":"Stir in diced onions, bell peppers, anaheim chile and jalapeño pepper.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cook until vegetables start to soften, approximately 5 minutes.","name":"Cook until vegetables start to soften, approximately 5 minutes.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-5"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Add ground turkey and garlic cloves to the vegetables and cook until meat is mostly browned.","name":"Add ground turkey and garlic cloves to the vegetables and cook until meat is mostly browned.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-6"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Season with chile powder, cumin and salt.","name":"Season with chile powder, cumin and salt.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-7"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Mix in beans, tomato sauce, diced tomatoes, chipotle chile and canned green chiles.","name":"Mix in beans, tomato sauce, diced tomatoes, chipotle chile and canned green chiles.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-8"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"If your coals are too hot you might need more water.","name":"If your coals are too hot you might need more water.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-9"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Allow chili to simmer for at least 30 min or up to several hours. The longer the chili cooks, the more flavor the chili will have. If you are simmering the chili for hours, remove 10-15 coals from underneath the Dutch oven. Keep an eye on the coals and the heat while it cooks. You may need to to add new coals if the old ones die out.","name":"Allow chili to simmer for at least 30 min or up to several hours. The longer the chili cooks, the more flavor the chili will have. If you are simmering the chili for hours, remove 10-15 coals from underneath the Dutch oven. Keep an eye on the coals and the heat while it cooks. You may need to to add new coals if the old ones die out.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-10"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Mix together (per package directions 1 box of cornbread mix. There are brands that only require water to be added.","name":"Mix together (per package directions 1 box of cornbread mix. There are brands that only require water to be added.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-11"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Spread cornbread batter evenly over the top of your chili.","name":"Spread cornbread batter evenly over the top of your chili.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-12"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cover Dutch oven with lid and place approximately 16 hot coals on the lid.","name":"Cover Dutch oven with lid and place approximately 16 hot coals on the lid.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-13"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Allow chili and cornbread to cook until cornbread is browned and done, approximately 20-30 minutes.","name":"Allow chili and cornbread to cook until cornbread is browned and done, approximately 20-30 minutes.","url":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#wprm-recipe-15548-step-0-14"}],"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":"4.67","ratingCount":"21","reviewCount":"1"},"review":[{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Laura,\r\n\r\nGreat \"Pot\" for a potluck.  My Dutch oven recipe was already started with a Mexican\/Chili theme.  Below\/in the Jalapeno cornbread...3 cups Roasted Corn with Chili Lime , onions and cheese.  I set out to top with tortilla strips...but did'.t have time to make or purchase.  Jalapeno Corn bread was perfect, and this was my first integrated Dutch oven attempt!\r\n\r\nTopped with Cilantro, diced onions, and Avocado and more Roasted Corn.  Visually appealing, perfect on a cool evening.  This will be a new tailgating go to.\r\n\r\nThe first empty Pot is always the best Compliment.  And it's great to only take one to an event.  Great Recipe, thank you.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"David K. Starnes"},"datePublished":"2017-10-28"}],"recipeCategory":["Recipes"],"recipeCuisine":["American"],"keywords":"campfire chili, camping recipe, chili and cornbread, chili with cornbread crust, cowboy chili, dutch oven chili, dutch oven cornbread","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","servingSize":"1 bowl","calories":"213 kcal","carbohydrateContent":"21 g","proteinContent":"25 g","fatContent":"4 g","saturatedFatContent":"1 g","transFatContent":"0.01 g","cholesterolContent":"47 mg","sodiumContent":"859 mg","fiberContent":"8 g","sugarContent":"6 g","unsaturatedFatContent":"3 g"},"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#recipe","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/#article"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https:\/\/familyspice.com\/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3\/"}]}</script>
