<h2 id="ingredients-needed"   class="wp-block-heading" >Ingredients needed</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-attachment-id="43468" data-permalink="https://familyspice.com/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2/" data-orig-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,1800" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-683x1024.jpg" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Ingredients labeled and needed to make campfire chili with cornbread." class="wp-image-43468" data-lazy-srcset="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2.jpg 1200w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-360x540.jpg 360w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-720x1080.jpg 720w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-180x270.jpg 180w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-300x450.jpg 300w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-attachment-id="43468" data-permalink="https://familyspice.com/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2/" data-orig-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,1800" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-683x1024.jpg" src="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2.jpg" alt="Ingredients labeled and needed to make campfire chili with cornbread." class="wp-image-43468" srcset="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2.jpg 1200w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-360x540.jpg 360w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-720x1080.jpg 720w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-180x270.jpg 180w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/campfire-chili-ingredients-1200-2-300x450.jpg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Ground meat:</strong> You can use either ground beef, ground pork or ground turkey. You can also combine meats for more flavor.</li>



<li><strong>Peppers:</strong> I use a combination of red bell peppers, anaheim chile and jalapeños. Anaheim chiles are mild. If you want more heat, try medium or hot hatch chiles. If you do not want anything spicy, omit the jalapeño.</li>



<li><strong>Chipotle chile in adobo sauce:</strong> OMG this stuff is AMAZING! Yes, it is spicy but it is also smokey and has incredible flavor. Use sparingly if you don&#8217;t like spicy, but try not to omit altogether.</li>



<li><strong>Canned green chiles:</strong> This is optional, but by using a variety of different chiles and peppers your chili base will have incredible flavor.  </li>



<li><strong>Extra virgin olive oil:</strong> I cook exclusively with olive oil. This is used for sautéing so you can use canola, corn, avocado or any other vegetable oil. </li>



<li><strong>Onion:</strong> You can use white or yellow onions.</li>



<li><strong>Garlic:</strong> I used fresh garlic, but since we&#8217;re camping, you could substitute with ½-1 teaspoon of garlic powder.</li>



<li><strong>Spices: </strong>Chile powder (mild or hot), cumin and salt.</li>



<li><strong>Canned beans:</strong> There is a huge debate on whether beans belong in chili. Me? I&#8217;m part of the pro-bean camp! I have used black beans, red kidney beans and even pinto beans. </li>



<li><strong>Pantry staples:</strong> Canned tomato sauce and canned diced tomatoes.</li>



<li><strong>Cornbread mix:</strong> To make camp cooking easier, I used a box mix of cornbread that only required water. I found <a data-lasso-id="443" data-lasso-name="Marie Callender's Original Cornbread Mix - 5 lbs. bag" href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0045ZA2JA/?tag=familyspice07-20" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener">Marie Callendar&#8217;s just-add-water cornbread mix</a> and it was fabulous with our chili.</li>



<li><strong>Toppings:</strong> Serve with shredded cheese, sour cream, cilantro, green onions and diced avocado with lime.</li>
</ul>



<h2 id="step-by-step-directions"   class="wp-block-heading" >Step-by-step directions</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1200" data-attachment-id="43462" data-permalink="https://familyspice.com/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3/do-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200/" data-orig-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,1200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-1024x1024.jpg" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Collage of four images showing how to make chili in a cast iron Dutch oven." class="wp-image-43462" data-lazy-srcset="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200.jpg 1200w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-360x360.jpg 360w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-180x180.jpg 180w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-768x768.jpg 768w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-500x500.jpg 500w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-720x720.jpg 720w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-300x300.jpg 300w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-100x100.jpg 100w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1200" data-attachment-id="43462" data-permalink="https://familyspice.com/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3/do-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200/" data-orig-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,1200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-1024x1024.jpg" src="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200.jpg" alt="Collage of four images showing how to make chili in a cast iron Dutch oven." class="wp-image-43462" srcset="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200.jpg 1200w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-360x360.jpg 360w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-180x180.jpg 180w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-768x768.jpg 768w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-500x500.jpg 500w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-720x720.jpg 720w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-300x300.jpg 300w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps1-1200-100x100.jpg 100w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<ol class="wp-block-list is-style-circle-number-list">
<li><strong>Prepare the coals. </strong>The key to successful Dutch oven cooking is to control the heat. Light up the coal briquettes and get them good and ready in about 20 minutes. This is all prepared in the campfire ring, so you can also do with this with the ash and coals from your wood.</li>
</ol>
