<p class="has-feast-branding-color-accents-background-color has-background">Remember not to place the Dutch oven&nbsp;directly over the flames, otherwise it can crack. Under each pot I had approximately 18 briquettes. You can also light a wood fire first and then lay the briquettes over the ash to get more heat.</p>



<ol start="2" class="wp-block-list is-style-circle-number-list">
<li><strong>Sauté the veggies.</strong> Add oil to the hot Dutch oven then add the chopped onions, peppers and chiles that you are using. Once the vegetables are softened, add your ground meat.</li>



<li><strong>Brown the meat.</strong> Break down the meat while it cooks. Add your seasonings.</li>
</ol>



<ol start="3" class="wp-block-list is-style-circle-number-list">
<li><strong>Break out the cans.</strong> Mix in beans, tomato sauce, diced tomatoes, chipotle in adobo and canned green chiles</li>
</ol>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1200" data-attachment-id="43463" data-permalink="https://familyspice.com/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3/do-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200/" data-orig-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,1200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-1024x1024.jpg" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Collage of four images showing how to make cornbread and chili in a cast iron Dutch oven." class="wp-image-43463" data-lazy-srcset="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200.jpg 1200w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-360x360.jpg 360w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-180x180.jpg 180w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-768x768.jpg 768w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-500x500.jpg 500w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-720x720.jpg 720w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-300x300.jpg 300w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-100x100.jpg 100w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1200" data-attachment-id="43463" data-permalink="https://familyspice.com/campfire-chili-with-cornbread-crust-3/do-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200/" data-orig-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200.jpg" data-orig-size="1200,1200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-1024x1024.jpg" src="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200.jpg" alt="Collage of four images showing how to make cornbread and chili in a cast iron Dutch oven." class="wp-image-43463" srcset="https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200.jpg 1200w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-360x360.jpg 360w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-180x180.jpg 180w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-768x768.jpg 768w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-500x500.jpg 500w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-720x720.jpg 720w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-300x300.jpg 300w, https://familyspice.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/DO-cornbread-chili-steps2-1200-100x100.jpg 100w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<ol start="4" class="wp-block-list is-style-circle-number-list">
<li><strong>Simmer.</strong> Allow chili to simmer for at least 30 min or up to several hours. The longer the chili cooks, the more flavor the chili will have. Add more hot coals as you need them.</li>



<li><strong>Bake cornbread.</strong> When your chili is almost ready, mix up the cornbread batter per package directions. Spread cornbread batter evenly over the top of your chili. Cover Dutch oven with lid and place approximately 16 hot coals on the lid. Allow chili and cornbread to cook until cornbread is browned and done, approximately 20-30 minutes.</li>
</ol>



<h2 id="recipe-tips-and-faqs"   class="wp-block-heading">Recipe tips and FAQs</h2>



<p>You can also use your cornbread mix to whip up some bacon <a href="https://familyspice.com/bacon-cornbread-pancakes/">cornbread pancakes</a> instead. All you need is a cast iron skillet!</p>



<p>You could also make this at home with an oven safe pot. Just make the chili the same way and pour your cornbread mix on top. Put the whole pot in your oven and bake it uncovered per your cornbread recipes directions.</p>



<p>If you want a real chile pepper chili and with a homemade cornbread crust that is crazy good, you can find THAT recipe is in my new cookbook, <em>The Camp &amp; Cabin Cookbook</em> (Countryman Press 2018). I have 100 recipes that are all prepared outdoors and over fire using multiple techniques, including the beloved Dutch oven.&nbsp;Learn more about my <a href="https://familyspice.com/camp-cabin-cookbook/" data-lasso-id="444">camping cookbook!</a></p>



<p>I have lots of wonderful dutch oven recipes here on my blog, too, like <a href="https://familyspice.com/chicken-cacciatore/">chicken cacciatore</a> or my&nbsp;<a href="https://familyspice.com/dutch-oven-italian-stuffed-peppers/">Italian stuffed peppers</a>. You can also bake in a dutch oven so be sure to try my  <a data-lasso-id="425" href="https://familyspice.com/campfire-pineapple-upside-down-cake/">pineapple upside down cake</a> and this <a data-lasso-id="426" href="https://familyspice.com/peach-crisp-almonds/">peach crisp</a>. </p>



<p>You can make almost anything in a Dutch oven!</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
