</div>
    <div class="wpd-reply-to">
    <i class='far fa-comments'></i>
    Reply to&nbsp;
    <a href="#comment-94842">
        Kasha
    </a>
</div>
    <div class="wpd-comment-text">
    <p>Hi Kasha-<br />
You can use mild chile peppers and powders and it won&#8217;t be spicy at all. If you have someone who is super sensitive you can skip the jalapeño, but remember they aren&#8217;t super spicy. The chipotle chile in adobo sauce can be spicy, but it adds so much delicious smokiness. So you can either skip it or just add a little of the sauce. All the different kinds of peppers and chiles offer a different flavor profile, but only a few are spicy. I hope your family likes it!<br />
Laura</p>

</div>
